# PostgreSQL

## Mục tiêu

PostgreSQL là một object-relational database system nổi tiếng với tính năng phong phú, extensibility xuất sắc, và compliance với SQL standards. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, PostgreSQL là lựa chọn ưu tiên cho các ứng dụng enterprise đòi hỏi ACID compliance nghiêm ngặt, advanced data types, và khả năng mở rộng linh hoạt. Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers và DBAs trong việc khai thác tối đa các khả năng của PostgreSQL một cách hiệu quả và an toàn.

PostgreSQL rule tập trung vào các features đặc trưng của PostgreSQL như JSONB data type, Full-Text Search, Window Functions, CTEs, Advanced Indexing (GIN, GiST, BRIN), PostGIS extension cho spatial data, và pgvector extension cho vector similarity search. Các best practices cho performance tuning, connection management, và operational excellence cũng được cover chi tiết.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Schema Design Principles**

Sử dụng appropriate data types cho columns. VARCHAR(n) cho variable length strings với known maximum. TEXT cho unlimited length text. BOOLEAN thay vì INTEGER flags. ARRAY cho collections of homogeneous items. JSONB cho semi-structured data. UUID thay vì serial integers cho distributed systems. ENUM được defined as types for reusable sets. Domain types cho reusable constraints.

**2. Index Strategy**

B-tree indexes cho equality và range queries. GIN indexes cho JSONB, arrays, và full-text search. GiST indexes cho geometric data và range types. BRIN indexes cho sequential data (time-series). Partial indexes cho subsets of rows. Covering indexes với INCLUDED columns. Expression indexes cho computed columns. Indexes được monitored cho usage và bloat.

**3. Query Optimization**

EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) cho detailed query analysis. Statistics được updated via ANALYZE. JOIN order impacts performance significantly. Subqueries in FROM được flatten automatically. Lateral joins cho correlated subqueries. UNION vs UNION ALL - avoid DISTINCT when possible. Window functions replace many subqueries. CTEs improve readability, may enable query optimization.

**4. JSON/JSONB Usage**

JSONB for frequently accessed JSON data. JSON for archival data rarely queried. GIN index on JSONB columns for search. JSONPath for querying (PostgreSQL 13+). Use operators: -> vs ->> vs #>. jsonb_each for unnesting. jsonb_set for updates. JSONB preserves key order và whitespace.

**5. Connection Management**

Use connection pooler: PgBouncer or pgpool-II. Transaction pooling vs session pooling based on needs. max_connections configured based on memory. connection_idle_timeout for cleanup. keepalives configured. Unix domain sockets preferred on same host. SSL connections for remote hosts.

**6. Performance Tuning**

shared_buffers: 25% of RAM for dedicated DB. effective_cache_size: 75% of RAM. work_mem: memory for sorting/hashing. maintenance_work_mem: for VACUUM, CREATE INDEX. random_page_cost: 1.1 for SSD, 4.0 for HDD. effective_io_concurrency for parallel queries. max_worker_processes for parallelism.

**7. Concurrency Control**

MVCC handles concurrent access automatically. VACUUM runs regularly to reclaim space. Autovacuum tuned for workload characteristics. Row-level locking for UPDATE/DELETE. SELECT FOR UPDATE for explicit locking. Advisory locks for application-level locking. REPEATABLE READ vs READ COMMITTED isolation levels.

**8. Full-Text Search**

tsvector column with trigger for automatic updates. GIN index on tsvector. tsquery for search expressions. Configurations: english, simple, or custom. Phrase search với to_tsquery. Ranking với ts_rank. Highlight với ts_headline.

**9. Backup và Recovery**

pg_dump for logical backups. pg_basebackup for physical. Point-in-time recovery via WAL archiving. Continuous archiving to object storage. Backup compression và encryption. Regular restore testing. pgBackRest for advanced backup management.

**10. Replication Setup**

Streaming replication for read replicas. Logical replication for cross-database. Synchronous vs asynchronous replication. Synchronous commit for durability. Replication slots prevent WAL accumulation. Monitoring replication lag. Cascading replication for multiple replicas.

## Checklist

- [ ] Data types được selected appropriately
- [ ] Index strategy được documented
- [ ] Query analysis performed với EXPLAIN
- [ ] Connection pooling configured
- [ ] Autovacuum tuned
- [ ] Full-text search indexed
- [ ] Backup strategy implemented
- [ ] Replication configured if needed
- [ ] Monitoring setup
- [ ] Security configured
- [ ] Documentation complete

## Anti Pattern

**1. Serial Primary Keys in Distributed Systems**

Serial integers don't scale across regions. They reveal business metrics. Sequence exhaustion possible. Solution: Use UUID v7 hoặc other time-ordered identifiers.

**2. Storing JSON in TEXT Column**

Treating JSON as blob without querying it. Full table scan for JSON queries. Cannot index effectively. Solution: Use JSONB with GIN index.

**3. Ignoring VACUUM**

Bloat accumulates, performance degrades. Transaction ID wraparound risk. Solution: Proper autovacuum configuration và monitoring.

**4. Over-indexing**

Many indexes on write-heavy tables. Index bloat affects insert performance. Storage waste. Solution: Regular index review và removal of unused.

**5. No Connection Pooling**

Each request creates new connection. Connection overhead high. Server overwhelmed with connections. Solution: Use PgBouncer or similar.

## Best Practice

**1. Use Generated Columns**

CREATE TABLE t (a int, b int, sum int GENERATED ALWAYS AS (a + b) STORED);
Generated columns are always consistent.

**2. Partition Large Tables**

CREATE TABLE sales (...) PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at);
Partitions improve query performance và maintenance.

**3. Materialized Views**

CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW monthly_sales AS SELECT ...;
Refresh on schedule or on demand.
Use with CONCURRENTLY for no blocking reads.

**4. Row-Level Security**

Enable RLS for multi-tenant applications.
CREATE POLICY tenant_policy ON orders USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')::int);

**5. Foreign Data Wrappers**

Access remote databases as if local.
Use postgres_fdw for cross-database queries.

**6. Custom Functions**

CREATE FUNCTION using PL/pgSQL, PL/v8, or other languages.
Use IMMUTABLE for functions that always return same result for same input.

**7. Advisory Locks**

For distributed locking without external tools.
SELECT pg_advisory_lock(123456789);
Release after use.

**8. Range Types**

For intervals: int4range, daterange, tsrange.
Use exclusion constraints: EXCLUDE USING gist (daterange WITH &&).

## Workflow

**Phase 1: Design**

Design schema with appropriate types. Plan indexing strategy. Define constraints và triggers. Document relationships.

**Phase 2: Development**

Write queries with EXPLAIN ANALYZE. Use CTEs for readability. Implement data access layer. Add migrations.

**Phase 3: Optimization**

Profile slow queries. Adjust indexes. Tune configuration. Consider partitioning.

**Phase 4: Deployment**

Run migrations in order. Verify performance. Load test. Monitor in production.

**Phase 5: Operations**

Monitor performance metrics. Regular VACUUM và ANALYZE. Backup validation. Capacity planning.

## Ví dụ

**Ví dụ 1: Advanced Schema with JSONB**

```sql
CREATE TYPE order_status AS ENUM ('pending', 'processing', 'shipped', 'delivered', 'cancelled');

CREATE TABLE orders (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  customer_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES customers(id),
  order_number VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
  status order_status NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
  items JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',
  metadata JSONB DEFAULT '{}',
  shipping_addresses JSONB,
  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),
  completed_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE
);

CREATE INDEX idx_orders_customer ON orders(customer_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_status ON orders(status);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_created ON orders(created_at DESC);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_items ON orders USING GIN (items);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_items_product ON orders USING GIN ((items -> 'product_id'));

-- Function to calculate order total
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION calculate_order_total(order_data JSONB)
RETURNS DECIMAL AS $$
DECLARE
  total DECIMAL := 0;
  item JSONB;
BEGIN
  FOR item IN SELECT * FROM jsonb_array_elements(order_data)
  LOOP
    total := total + (item ->> 'quantity')::DECIMAL * (item ->> 'price')::DECIMAL;
  END LOOP;
  RETURN total;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql IMMUTABLE;
```

**Ví dụ 2: Full-Text Search**

```sql
-- Add search vector column
ALTER TABLE articles ADD COLUMN search_vector tsvector;

CREATE INDEX idx_articles_search ON articles USING GIN(search_vector);

-- Trigger to update search vector
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION articles_search_trigger()
RETURNS trigger AS $$
BEGIN
  NEW.search_vector := 
    setweight(to_tsvector('english', coalesce(NEW.title, '')), 'A') ||
    setweight(to_tsvector('english', coalesce(NEW.content, '')), 'B') ||
    setweight(to_tsvector('english', coalesce(NEW.author, '')), 'C');
  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

CREATE TRIGGER articles_search_update
  BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE ON articles
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION articles_search_trigger();

-- Search function
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION search_articles(query TEXT, limit_count INT DEFAULT 10)
RETURNS TABLE(id UUID, title TEXT, author TEXT, rank REAL) AS $$
BEGIN
  RETURN QUERY
  SELECT a.id, a.title, a.author,
         ts_rank(search_vector, websearch_to_tsquery('english', query)) AS rank
  FROM articles
  WHERE search_vector @@ websearch_to_tsquery('english', query)
  ORDER BY rank DESC
  LIMIT limit_count;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

**Ví dụ 3: Row-Level Security**

```sql
-- Enable RLS
ALTER TABLE orders ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Create policy
CREATE POLICY tenant_orders ON orders
  FOR ALL
  TO authenticated
  USING (customer_id IN (
    SELECT id FROM customers WHERE tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant')::UUID
  ));

-- Application sets tenant context
SET app.current_tenant = 'tenant-uuid-here';
```

